---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="UAE Residency Visas"
  description="An overview of UAE residency routes — from standard employment and property visas to the long-term Golden Visa — and how to think about which one fits your situation."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Residency</p>
    <h1>Finding a long-term home in the UAE</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most people who start researching UAE residency aren't chasing a
      specific visa programme by name — they're looking for a stable,
      long-term place to live, with a process that's clear and doesn't need
      re-doing every year or two. This page is a map of the actual routes,
      starting from that question rather than from visa terminology.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The routes, in plain terms</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Typical duration</th><th>Who it fits</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Employment visa</td>
            <td>Tied to employment contract, typically 2–3 years</td>
            <td>Anyone relocating for a UAE-based job</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Property investor visa</td>
            <td>Typically 2 years, renewable</td>
            <td>Property owners above a set investment threshold</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/golden-visa/">Golden Visa</a></td>
            <td>5 or 10 years, renewable</td>
            <td>
              Larger property investors, business owners, and other
              qualifying categories — the route most people asking about
              long-term stability actually want
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Why the Golden Visa is usually the right question to ask</h2>
    <p>
      If what you actually want is not to think about your residency status
      again for a decade — rather than renewing paperwork every couple of
      years — the Golden Visa is the route built for that. The
      <a href="/golden-visa/">Golden Visa page</a> covers eligibility,
      thresholds, and the property-investment route specifically; the
      <a href="/family-lifestyle/">family and lifestyle page</a> covers what
      changes day to day once you have it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

